---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';import {evidence,url} from '../lib/data';
import retrieval from '../../data/raw/retrieval-manifest.json';
const downloads=[['policies','Policy inventory'],['legal_status_history','Legal status history'],['claim_source_ledger','Claim-to-source ledger'],['sources','Source catalog'],['agency_year','Agency / reporting records'],['species_year','Species / research records'],['cases','Selected enforcement cases'],['facility_year','Facility-year schema (no observations)'],['observations','All observations'],['evidence_gaps','Known evidence gaps']];
---
<Layout title="Sources and downloads"><div class="eyebrow">Inspect and reproduce</div><h1>Follow every claim<br/>back to its source.</h1><p class="lede">Statutes and court opinions establish legal changes. Agency records document reported implementation. Audits and research help test what those records can tell us about animals.</p><section class="section"><h2>Download the evidence</h2><p class="small">CSV files are UTF-8; array fields contain JSON. Empty numeric cells mean missing, not zero. The facility-year file intentionally has a schema but no rows because a validated longitudinal panel was not assembled.</p><div class="download-grid">{downloads.map(([name,label])=><a href={url(`data/${name}.csv`)} download>{label} ↓ CSV</a>)}<a href={url('data/evidence.json')} download>Complete evidence package ↓ JSON</a><a href={url('data/analysis.json')} download>Reproducible calculations ↓ JSON</a><a href={url('data/curated-manifest.json')} download>Curated file hashes ↓ JSON</a><a href={url('data/retrieval-manifest.json')} download>Source retrieval results & hashes ↓ JSON</a></div></section>
<section class="section"><h2>Source explorer</h2><p class="small">Automated retrieval is separate from reading a source through indexed text. Some publishers deny scripted access or return alternate content. See the retrieval log for HTTP status and hashes; no restriction was bypassed.</p><details><summary>Automated retrieval limitations</summary><ul>{retrieval.filter(r=>r.status!==200||r.error).map(r=><li><a href={`#${r.sourceId}`}>{r.sourceId}</a>: {r.status===null?'Network error':`HTTP ${r.status}`} — {r.error||'Nonstandard response; source content not established by this retrieval.'}</li>)}</ul></details><label class="control chart-control">Search title, publisher, evidence type or locator<input id="source-search" type="search" placeholder="Try USDA, statute, peer-reviewed…"/></label><p id="source-count" class="small" aria-live="polite">{evidence.sources.length} sources</p>{evidence.sources.map((s:any)=><article class="source-item" id={s.id} data-source data-text={`${s.title} ${s.publisher} ${s.evidenceType} ${s.locator}`.toLowerCase()}><span class="tag">{s.evidenceType}</span><h3><a href={s.url}>{s.title}</a></h3><p><b>{s.publisher}</b> · Published {s.publicationDate||'date not identified'} · Accessed {s.accessDate}</p><p><b>Relevant passage:</b> {s.locator}</p><p><b>Limit:</b> {s.limitations}</p><p class="small">Independent verification: {s.independentlyVerified?'Recorded':'Not independently replicated'}. {s.verificationNote}</p><details><summary>Claims using this source</summary>{evidence.claims.filter((c:any)=>c.sourceIds.includes(s.id)).map((c:any)=><p>{c.claim} {c.policyId&&<a href={url(`policies/${c.policyId}/`)}>Policy detail →</a>}</p>)}</details></article>)}</section>
<script>const input=document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('#source-search')!;input.addEventListener('input',()=>{let n=0;document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-source]').forEach(el=>{el.hidden=!el.dataset.text!.includes(input.value.toLowerCase());if(!el.hidden)n++});document.querySelector('#source-count')!.textContent=`${n} sources match`});</script></Layout>
